  "experiment": "dilute10 -- the 1:10 diluted-target rerun",
  "freematch_nb3_rule": "Before bundle v3 is built, FreeMatch × nb3 receives the same label-free 300-step measurement as §7.47, with its real 1:10 frozen heads on folds 1–4 and a known-null (original mode reproduces its recorded early behaviour). If on every fold the recovery step is ≤ 150 (10% of its 1500-step budget) and at least 270 of 300 updates are applied, with every loss and weight finite, FreeMatch × nb3 runs exactly as pre-registered. Otherwise nothing further runs, and the author decides.",
  "no_verdict_rule": "For CORAL × nb3 and FreeMatch × nb3 (the two stages that start from new 1:10 frozen heads): if a run applies fewer than 50% of its budget's optimiser updates (GradScaler skips counted as not applied), it is reported as a numerical failure under the pre-registered protocol, and that arm receives no branch verdict (part 1 §7). Its values are reported descriptively. Each run's skip count and applied fraction are reported regardless.",
